Sogen (debug, not for upstream): trace the exceptions, the spent stack, the errors

For a few runs of nodecode's spike. SOGEN_TRACE_EXCEPTIONS=1 makes Sogen
print its exception ring when a run ends; this keeps 512 instead of 32
and prints them when the run stops on a host error too, which a guest
that runs off its stack's end does. A stack overflow also prints the code
addresses that occur most on the stack between the stack pointer and the
stack's top: module+offset for loaded images, the raw address for SBCL's
spaces. And a system call that answers with an error status is logged
with its first three arguments, the first 20 of each call and status;
a failed open also names what it looked up (the first 300 of those).
Each ALPC port a guest connects is named, a port nothing serves says so,
and each RPC call is logged with its interface, opnum, transfer syntax,
and the first bytes of its request and reply (the first 40 per
interface).

